   they are served inside a network service. lynceus.detector (our own decoder)
   does not import Ultralytics.

2. RealWaste training data (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 treated as binding)
   Fine-tuned on RealWaste by S. Single, S. Iranmanesh and R. Raad (University
   of Wollongong), UCI Machine Learning Repository id 908,
   DOI 10.24432/C5SS4G. The UCI page states CC BY 4.0; the README inside the
   dataset zip states CC BY-NC-SA 4.0. Until the authors clarify, the stricter
   terms (attribution, non-commercial, share-alike) are treated as binding for
   the dataset and, conservatively, for these weights.
   See backend/benchmark/images/ATTRIBUTION.md.

3. TACO training data (annotations CC BY 4.0)
   Also fine-tuned on the TACO train/val splits: "TACO: Trash Annotations in
   Context" by P. F. Proença and P. Simões, github.com/pedropro/TACO. The
   annotations are CC BY 4.0; the photos are hosted on Flickr under their
   uploaders' licences. No TACO image is stored in this repository.

Corresponding source
   The complete training and export source for these weights is in ml/ of this
   repository (ml/README.md: fetch_realwaste.py, fetch_taco.py,
   build_dataset.py, train.py, colab_train.sh, export_onnx.py). This is our offer of the corresponding source under
   AGPL-3.0 section 13 to anyone who interacts with a service running them.

Commercial use
   These weights are for evaluation and non-commercial use. Commercial use
   requires both (a) retraining on data you have the rights to (not RealWaste)
   and (b) an Ultralytics Enterprise licence, or replacing the detector with a
   permissively licensed one. Point DETECTOR_MODEL_PATH at the replacement, or
   set it empty to run without the detector.
